# Firebase service-account keys (docs/DECISIONS.md D-059)
#
# These are ADMIN credentials: one grants the ability to send push to every
# device registered to the project, and they do not expire on their own. The
# file Google hands you is named like
# `habita-ai-97928-firebase-adminsdk-xxxxx-0123456789.json`, which matches
# nothing above, so it would otherwise be committed by a plain `git add -A`.
#
# `scripts/send-test-push.js` takes the path to one as an argument precisely so
# the key never has to live in the repo — keep it outside the project directory.
#
# NOT ignored, deliberately: `android/app/google-services.json` (client config,
# already tracked, safe to commit — it ships inside the APK anyway) and
# `firebase.json` (build config, must be committed or the notification channel
# id is empty and Android 8+ drops every backgrounded message).
*serviceAccount*.json
*service-account*.json
*-adminsdk-*.json
*firebase-adminsdk*.json
serviceAccountKey.json
# Apple push keys, for when iOS lands (M4-T10)
*.p8
